WEBVTT

00:01:35.870 --> 00:01:37.680
Good morning, Onii-chan.

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:39.410
What's for breakfast?

00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:42.290
A calcium packed omelet.

00:01:42.290 --> 00:01:43.410
What's that?

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:44.980
It's got egg shells in it.

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:46.350
What?

00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:49.110
We're out of eggs.

00:01:49.110 --> 00:01:50.350
Okay.

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:53.890
Onii-chan, leave breakfast to me.

00:01:53.890 --> 00:01:58.900
Indigo Pressure

00:01:54.770 --> 00:01:56.970
Thanks for the food.

00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:01.600
Is this what you meant
by leave it to me?

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:03.660
It can't hurt once in a while.

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:04.850
I suppose not.

00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:06.430
It's a good change of pace.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:11.080
It's not like you to be so irritable.

00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:15.740
You're supposed to be absent minded.

00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:17.320
Hey.

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:21.290
Delicious.

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:23.750
Eat up, Onii-chan.

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:31.130
I can't get any lower if I need your help.

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:34.930
Come on. We'll be late if we don't hurry.

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:44.300
Wow.

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:49.950
People who drive like that tend
to be mild mannered.

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:52.780
Good morning.

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:54.610
Morning.

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:56.280
Good morning.

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:57.370
Good morning.

00:02:57.790 --> 00:03:00.140
You're looking a little rough
around the edges.

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:00.750
Huh?

00:03:01.210 --> 00:03:03.710
Kamikura-sensei, you're easy to read.

00:03:03.710 --> 00:03:05.520
Really?

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:07.730
Tomoko-chan, you've got a keen eye.

00:03:07.730 --> 00:03:09.830
Don't let it get you down.

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:13.080
Elis-chan, why don't you
come over tonight?

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:15.120
I redecorated my room.

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:17.510
You mean you made it even lovelier?

00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:19.010
You'll have to see for yourself.

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:21.260
Onii-chan, you heard her.

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:23.270
You don't need to make
me dinner tonight.

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:25.050
I'll see you in the club
room after school.

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:41.500
Here.

00:03:42.770 --> 00:03:44.000
Thanks.

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:46.260
Running by yourself?

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:49.510
Yeah. I just felt like running.

00:03:49.510 --> 00:03:52.770
You've always gone running
by yourself when

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:54.680
something was bothering you.

00:03:55.850 --> 00:03:57.240
What's bothering you now?

00:03:57.720 --> 00:03:58.980
I'm sorry.

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:01.760
Shin-chan told me everything.

00:04:02.170 --> 00:04:03.200
I didn't know.

00:04:03.650 --> 00:04:09.000
I attacked you and insensitively
told you to paint.

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:10.440
I...

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:12.270
You don't have to apologize.

00:04:12.570 --> 00:04:13.230
But...

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:20.390
It's not your fault or Yanagi's
fault I stopped drawing.

00:04:20.390 --> 00:04:21.190
Hiroki.

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:23.540
I didn't stop drawing because
I wanted to.

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:25.990
I stopped because I couldn't
draw any more.

00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:30.600
I didn't have trouble with my college
assignments or exercises...

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:34.600
but no matter what I did, I couldn't
create my own work.

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:41.910
I need to start working on my final painting,
but I haven't even started.

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:43.930
I see...

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:47.760
Sometimes I think it might
be a good thing, though.

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:50.850
The path to becoming an art
teacher has opened to me...

00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:52.900
and I really think I could enjoy teaching.

00:04:53.370 --> 00:04:56.430
Even you said I might make
a good teacher.

00:04:56.810 --> 00:04:57.840
Hiroki...

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:00.570
This is my problem.

00:05:00.970 --> 00:05:03.440
Don't blame yourself.

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:07.250
I can't stand to have you
worry about me.

00:05:09.860 --> 00:05:12.800
Well, I need to get to the faculty office.

00:05:13.170 --> 00:05:15.750
I'm sure you've got classes
to prepare for, too.

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:16.630
See you later.

00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:24.570
Kamikura-sensei.

00:05:25.210 --> 00:05:26.510
Good morning.

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:28.320
Good morning.

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:31.680
The superintendent was looking for you.

00:05:34.180 --> 00:05:35.050
Come in.

00:05:36.290 --> 00:05:37.970
Excuse me.

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:39.450
Is there something you wanted?

00:05:39.450 --> 00:05:43.980
Tomorrow we will be holding a meeting
to choose next year's special students...

00:05:43.980 --> 00:05:47.630
and I was hoping you would
attend, Kamikura-sensei.

00:05:48.670 --> 00:05:49.910
While there are no

00:05:49.910 --> 00:05:54.550
art students possessing the explosive
talent of this year's Hosen-san...

00:05:54.550 --> 00:05:58.620
if there are any who show promise,
please recommend them.

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:00.190
Yes.

00:06:00.190 --> 00:06:03.810
I was also considering inviting
Yanagi Shinichiro...

00:06:03.810 --> 00:06:06.480
to return next year as our
special guest lecturer.

00:06:06.740 --> 00:06:09.870
As a man who became a professional
artist at such a young age...

00:06:09.870 --> 00:06:12.980
the students seem to have
learned a lot from him.

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:17.620
I hope he inspired you as well.

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:21.030
What do you mean by that?

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:22.730
What?

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:28.230
I thought he might inspire
you to paint again.

00:06:28.230 --> 00:06:33.190
I will become an art teacher,
not an artist.

00:06:33.190 --> 00:06:36.170
Yanagi and I are not on the same path.

00:06:36.170 --> 00:06:37.610
I didn't mean...

00:06:38.030 --> 00:06:44.980
I simply thought you could create your
own paintings while teaching.

00:06:44.980 --> 00:06:48.150
You sound like you're suggesting
I find real employment...

00:06:48.150 --> 00:06:51.270
because I can't make a
living off my paintings.

00:06:51.270 --> 00:06:52.560
That is not what I meant.

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:56.730
A wealthy person like you
wouldn't understand!

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:03.550
I'm sorry. I said too much.

00:07:13.380 --> 00:07:15.200
Kamikura-sensei?

00:07:16.150 --> 00:07:17.610
Kamikura-sensei?

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:21.900
We discussed our plans for
the cultural festival...

00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:24.300
and we were hoping for your input.

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:25.960
Okay, I'll read it.

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:29.380
Is Kamikura-sensei all right?

00:07:29.710 --> 00:07:32.340
Sorry. Just give him some space.

00:07:33.110 --> 00:07:38.920
I know I said he's absent minded,
but he's gone too far.

00:07:38.920 --> 00:07:40.370
How interesting.

00:07:40.940 --> 00:07:42.380
What is?

00:07:42.380 --> 00:07:45.510
I'm not sure who is taking care of who.

00:07:45.510 --> 00:07:51.050
At first I thought you were a spoiled girl
who always needed her Onii-chan.

00:07:51.340 --> 00:07:53.830
I take advantage of Onii-chan's
kindness...

00:07:53.830 --> 00:07:56.280
but he's too easy on himself.

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:04.500
Did the vice principal want
to speak with you as well?

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:07.230
Yes. He asked me to oppose

00:08:07.230 --> 00:08:10.430
the increase of special students
at the meeting tomorrow.

00:08:10.430 --> 00:08:13.660
He must be more interested in
opposing the superintendent...

00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:16.300
than the addition of more
special students.

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:19.850
There are quite a few
teachers opposed to

00:08:19.850 --> 00:08:23.610
the new superintendent
for no apparent reason.

00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:33.500
Elis is at Fujinami's place,
and Kiri said she's busy.

00:08:33.910 --> 00:08:35.430
What am I going to do for dinner?

00:08:38.260 --> 00:08:39.530
Kamikura-sensei.

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:43.170
Are you on your way home?

00:08:43.170 --> 00:08:44.250
Yes.

00:08:44.250 --> 00:08:46.300
Would you like a ride?

00:08:46.300 --> 00:08:48.070
You don't need to do that.

00:08:48.590 --> 00:08:51.150
I'd like to continue our conversation
from this morning.

00:08:51.150 --> 00:08:51.840
Please.

00:08:58.900 --> 00:09:00.800
It looks like there's some traffic.

00:09:06.680 --> 00:09:07.890
I'm not in a hurry.

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:09.570
Leave it to me.

00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:14.500
Superintendent, you're a different
person behind the wheel.

00:09:14.860 --> 00:09:16.000
I wonder.

00:09:16.650 --> 00:09:18.410
Everyone seems to say that.

00:09:18.410 --> 00:09:19.740
Keep your eyes on the road...

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:23.270
Could you let me out in front
of that restaurant?

00:09:23.610 --> 00:09:25.940
I would be happy to drive you home.

00:09:25.940 --> 00:09:28.290
I'm on my own tonight...

00:09:28.290 --> 00:09:30.080
so I thought I'd get dinner
there before going home.

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:31.880
Oh, in that case...

00:09:40.070 --> 00:09:42.930
Do you eat here often?

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:45.470
Yes, I like this place.

00:09:45.470 --> 00:09:47.510
Here is the wine list.

00:09:47.880 --> 00:09:52.940
We happen to have a nice Bordeaux
you would like, Saginomiya-sama.

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:55.510
I'm driving today.

00:09:55.510 --> 00:09:58.440
I'll drive on the way home.

00:09:58.440 --> 00:09:59.560
But...

00:09:59.560 --> 00:10:01.480
Please, I insist.

00:10:02.590 --> 00:10:05.430
Then I will have the Bordeaux.

00:10:05.430 --> 00:10:07.050
Yes, ma'am.

00:10:09.270 --> 00:10:12.780
I feel bad for being the only
one drinking wine, and...

00:10:12.780 --> 00:10:16.330
I am sorry about this morning.

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:20.000
I said something rather inconsiderate.

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:23.020
No, I should be apologizing to you.

00:10:23.580 --> 00:10:24.860
I'm sorry.

00:10:25.910 --> 00:10:27.540
I was a little shocked.

00:10:27.860 --> 00:10:30.210
I am ashamed of my inexperience.

00:10:30.210 --> 00:10:32.280
Please don't worry about it.

00:10:32.740 --> 00:10:35.380
I was mostly just venting my anger.

00:10:36.420 --> 00:10:37.820
Venting?

00:10:37.820 --> 00:10:41.510
I'd been reminded of my
weakness all morning.

00:10:41.510 --> 00:10:43.660
I can't believe I said that to you.

00:10:44.270 --> 00:10:45.620
It's pathetic, really.

00:10:46.470 --> 00:10:48.660
I understand your feelings very well.

00:10:51.840 --> 00:10:53.220
Thank you for dinner.

00:10:53.220 --> 00:10:54.350
Not at all.

00:10:54.350 --> 00:10:57.970
Thank you for joining me.

00:10:59.340 --> 00:11:00.560
Are you all right?

00:11:00.560 --> 00:11:02.260
I'm sorry...

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:05.740
You're looking pretty shaky,
Superintendent.

00:11:05.740 --> 00:11:08.850
Thank you. I'll be fine.

00:11:15.050 --> 00:11:20.330
Superintendent, where do you live?

00:11:31.660 --> 00:11:32.780
Oh, right.

00:11:34.520 --> 00:11:36.670
Please select your route.

00:11:41.350 --> 00:11:44.850
Superintendent. Superintendent.

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:49.300
We're here.

00:11:53.090 --> 00:11:54.600
I'll park the car.

00:11:54.600 --> 00:11:56.490
Thank you.

00:11:58.650 --> 00:12:00.400
I'm going to get going.

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:03.310
I'll walk you to the station.

00:12:03.310 --> 00:12:05.140
I know the way.

00:12:05.140 --> 00:12:07.930
You should go lie down.

00:12:08.430 --> 00:12:11.080
You still seem to have some
alcohol in your system.

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:13.400
Get some rest.

00:12:36.320 --> 00:12:39.050
Sounds like you ended up eating
a fancy dinner yesterday.

00:12:39.050 --> 00:12:42.070
Yeah. It was great.

00:12:42.310 --> 00:12:46.870
Dinner with the beautiful, mature and
elegant acting superintendent.

00:12:47.270 --> 00:12:49.510
I bet the food wasn't bad, either.

00:12:50.530 --> 00:12:51.220
Hey.

00:12:52.420 --> 00:12:54.110
What's wrong with you?

00:12:54.110 --> 00:12:56.200
I want a fancy lunch.

00:12:56.650 --> 00:12:58.580
It's no fair if you're the only one.

00:12:58.580 --> 00:13:00.860
You're acting like a child again.

00:13:00.860 --> 00:13:06.040
I'll take you to whatever fancy restaurant
you want when you're older.

00:13:06.660 --> 00:13:07.530
But...

00:13:07.530 --> 00:13:08.630
What?

00:13:08.630 --> 00:13:12.570
The superintendent seemed exhausted.

00:13:13.200 --> 00:13:16.450
She's running this school
at such a young age.

00:13:16.450 --> 00:13:18.510
It's got to be a lot of work.

00:13:18.960 --> 00:13:25.160
Apparently there's a few teachers who don't
think very well of the superintendent.

00:13:25.160 --> 00:13:26.580
Really...

00:13:26.580 --> 00:13:29.950
That's why she blows off
steam after school.

00:13:43.430 --> 00:13:44.800
Kamikura-sensei.

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:48.840
I didn't know you were the
naginata club advisor.

00:13:50.130 --> 00:13:53.420
I have been doing this
since I was a student.

00:13:53.420 --> 00:13:54.710
I hope there's nothing wrong with that.

00:13:54.710 --> 00:13:59.210
No, I've just been intrigued by all
the unexpected sides of you

00:13:59.210 --> 00:14:01.100
I've seen since yesterday.

00:14:01.750 --> 00:14:02.690
Sorry.

00:14:02.690 --> 00:14:04.390
Intrigued...

00:14:04.390 --> 00:14:07.190
It was supposed to be a compliment.

00:14:07.190 --> 00:14:09.730
It doesn't feel like praise.

00:14:10.610 --> 00:14:11.660
Sorry.

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:14.600
I wasn't trying to accuse
you of anything.

00:14:14.600 --> 00:14:18.230
The meeting is about to start.

00:14:18.230 --> 00:14:20.540
I had forgotten all about it!

00:14:22.640 --> 00:14:24.610
I'll go as soon as I get changed.

00:14:35.680 --> 00:14:37.570
Sorry to make you wait.

00:14:40.100 --> 00:14:45.800
I would like to begin the selection meeting
of next year's special student.

00:14:46.600 --> 00:14:50.100
I would like to suggest increasing
the number of special students...

00:14:50.100 --> 00:14:52.130
from five to ten next year.

00:14:53.010 --> 00:14:59.810
We should provide as much support
as possible to promising students.

00:15:00.520 --> 00:15:05.030
Here is a list of potential candidates
I gathered from the teachers.

00:15:06.590 --> 00:15:10.040
Let us begin with the
special art student...

00:15:10.040 --> 00:15:11.570
Acting Superintendent.

00:15:12.190 --> 00:15:14.270
Vice Principal, what is it?

00:15:14.930 --> 00:15:18.310
Regarding the increase
of special students...

00:15:18.720 --> 00:15:24.400
We should focus on growing the
school's student body first.

00:15:24.740 --> 00:15:29.340
There is no benefit to increasing
the number of special students.

00:15:29.340 --> 00:15:33.610
Furthermore, many of the special
students are unique individuals...

00:15:33.610 --> 00:15:35.550
who can be quite a challenge to handle.

00:15:35.550 --> 00:15:37.050
Is he talking about Elis?

00:15:37.400 --> 00:15:39.720
What do you think, Acting
Superintendent?

00:15:40.650 --> 00:15:45.300
Nadesico Academy has always
strove to nurture...

00:15:45.300 --> 00:15:49.110
students with artistic
and athletic talents.

00:15:49.110 --> 00:15:52.920
I made my decision because I believe increasing
the number of special students...

00:15:52.920 --> 00:15:54.370
is in line with this direction.

00:15:55.620 --> 00:15:58.510
Do you agree with this, Principal?

00:15:59.700 --> 00:16:03.760
No. Not everyone at our school
agrees with that view.

00:16:03.760 --> 00:16:06.840
Then it is the acting superintendent's
arbitrary decision.

00:16:09.450 --> 00:16:13.020
What does the superintendent currently
abroad in France think?

00:16:13.020 --> 00:16:16.010
You've asked her for her
opinion, haven't you?

00:16:17.520 --> 00:16:21.880
I have not asked Superintendent
Saginomiya Ai for her opinion.

00:16:21.880 --> 00:16:25.130
I should have held a meeting
to discuss this measure.

00:16:25.840 --> 00:16:27.760
I am sorry.

00:16:30.410 --> 00:16:35.020
I agree with the acting
superintendent's idea.

00:16:35.530 --> 00:16:38.410
I used to draw once,

00:16:38.410 --> 00:16:41.180
and talent is something that grows
when we inspire each other.

00:16:41.180 --> 00:16:46.500
Shouldn't we accept as many promising
students as possible?

00:16:52.760 --> 00:16:56.130
While we can't accept all of them,

00:16:56.130 --> 00:16:59.810
I do believe increasing the number
of special students...

00:16:59.810 --> 00:17:01.500
and supporting their talents
would be a good thing.

00:17:02.830 --> 00:17:04.170
I agree.

00:17:06.010 --> 00:17:06.890
Me, too.

00:17:06.890 --> 00:17:08.060
I agree.

00:17:18.360 --> 00:17:19.480
Principal...

00:17:21.090 --> 00:17:25.540
It seems the majority of the faculty support
expanding the student body.

00:17:25.540 --> 00:17:27.200
Why don't we allow it?

00:17:27.200 --> 00:17:29.990
I would like to begin our discussion...

00:17:29.990 --> 00:17:33.160
with the idea of admitting ten
special students next year.

00:17:40.870 --> 00:17:43.700
I'm glad we got through
that meeting okay.

00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:44.640
Yeah.

00:17:44.640 --> 00:17:46.470
Hiroki, I was impressed.

00:17:47.410 --> 00:17:48.990
I was wrong about you.

00:17:48.990 --> 00:17:51.850
What did you think I was before?

00:17:52.250 --> 00:17:58.790
I'm amazed you expressed your opinion
so confidently in that setting.

00:17:58.790 --> 00:18:01.240
It was nothing.

00:18:01.640 --> 00:18:04.760
I just happened to agree with
the acting superintendent.

00:18:05.100 --> 00:18:07.200
Thank you.

00:18:11.690 --> 00:18:14.440
Yes, the meeting ended well.

00:18:14.440 --> 00:18:16.880
Really? I'm relieved.

00:18:17.410 --> 00:18:23.880
I'm not as good as you,
but I'm doing my best.

00:18:23.880 --> 00:18:25.320
Don't worry about me.

00:18:25.320 --> 00:18:30.750
I understand. I know it must be difficult,
but take care of Nadesico.

00:18:30.750 --> 00:18:32.890
Thank you. Good bye.

00:18:34.260 --> 00:18:36.260
That was my younger sister.

00:18:36.580 --> 00:18:39.230
She is the superintendent.

00:18:39.850 --> 00:18:41.550
Really.

00:18:42.120 --> 00:18:46.240
She is a very grounded person, and
I'm always being compared to her.

00:18:46.240 --> 00:18:51.320
But if I lose to that, I'll never make
it as the acting superintendent.

00:18:52.200 --> 00:18:55.490
Thank you for what you said earlier.

00:18:56.700 --> 00:18:58.250
I'm glad you did that.

00:18:58.250 --> 00:19:00.450
Superintendent!

00:19:00.450 --> 00:19:01.640
Yes.

00:19:48.070 --> 00:19:49.590
She's an amazing person.

00:19:50.080 --> 00:19:51.790
The acting superintendent?

00:19:51.790 --> 00:19:55.560
She's at home in fancy restaurants and
surrounded by expensive cars...

00:19:55.560 --> 00:19:57.870
but she goes to pubs and sings karaoke.

00:19:59.350 --> 00:20:01.870
Yeah. She might be a proud person...

00:20:01.870 --> 00:20:04.450
but she's got just the right
amount of pride.

00:20:06.600 --> 00:20:07.680
I'm next.

00:20:12.990 --> 00:20:14.220
I'm home.

00:20:14.220 --> 00:20:15.360
Welcome back.

00:20:15.760 --> 00:20:19.050
Elis, could you get me some water?

00:20:19.050 --> 00:20:21.270
Onii-chan, you smell like alcohol.

00:20:25.950 --> 00:20:27.400
Hey, Elis.

00:20:27.400 --> 00:20:28.510
What?

00:20:28.510 --> 00:20:34.680
I think I've been too easy on
myself this whole time.

00:20:35.690 --> 00:20:37.210
You finally noticed?

00:20:37.880 --> 00:20:39.390
Took you long enough.

00:20:40.380 --> 00:20:42.650
You're so absent minded.

00:20:42.650 --> 00:20:43.490
Here.

00:20:46.650 --> 00:20:47.820
Good night.

00:20:50.920 --> 00:20:52.670
She's more mature than me.

00:21:09.330 --> 00:21:10.510
Hiroki?

00:21:12.120 --> 00:21:16.330
I heard she was out with the
others until morning.

00:21:16.330 --> 00:21:17.730
Really?

00:21:18.910 --> 00:21:22.510
I should go check on the art club.

00:23:11.460 --> 00:23:13.660
Light purple is the color of maturity.

00:23:13.660 --> 00:23:17.220
A color with strength
and hidden kindness.

00:23:17.950 --> 00:23:19.210
Hey, Hiroki...

00:23:19.520 --> 00:23:22.250
Do hardworking women scare you away?

00:23:22.250 --> 00:23:24.080
I wouldn't say that, but...

00:23:24.080 --> 00:23:26.100
I'd be afraid of being lectured by her.

00:23:26.650 --> 00:23:29.090
Someone should set you straight
once in a while.

00:23:29.090 --> 00:23:30.920
I think I might cry.

00:23:30.920 --> 00:23:33.060
Get yourself together!

00:23:33.060 --> 00:23:36.450
Next episode, “Light Purple
All Night Long”

00:23:36.450 --> 00:23:38.460
Don't hound the ones you love!
